// The editor's own half of the game seam.
//
// The engine asks a *game* for these, as function values handed in through
// eng_seam (docs/IDML.md §2, engine's app.id). The editor is not a game -- it
// hosts other people's -- so it answers as a host: a `@name` in a previewed
// document reads that document's own variable, which is what makes a gate like
// `?@ready` mean anything in the panel. ed_boot11 (scn.id) is what hands these
// in; a program that answers 0 for everything, the way `stub/` once did, hid
// every gated panel in every game the editor opened, which looked like the UI
// having broken.
//
// The legacy reader is scr_get because the games the editor still opens are
// documents the engine interprets. When they become `id`, this becomes a lookup
// into the previewed program instead -- and the editor will have to run it.

g_ref(string name) {
  int ret_i = scr_get(0 - 1, name);
} return int ret_i;
given ed_t_boot stdin "" ("nope"):(0) then calls scr_get:(-1, "nope")
given ed_t_boot stdin "" ("score"):(0) then calls scr_get:(-1, "score")

g_act(string name) {
  lset((import ed_st), 17, 1);
} return void;
given ed_t_boot stdin "" ("foo"):() then ed_ntxt:("left drag: select   middle: pan   right: orbit   wheel: zoom")
given ed_t_boot stdin "" (""):() then ed_ntxt:("left drag: select   middle: pan   right: orbit   wheel: zoom")

g_stage(int k) {
  int ret_i = ed_gstage(k);
} return int ret_i;
given ed_t_boot stdin "" (0):(320) then calls ed_gstage:(0)
given ed_t_boot stdin "" (2):(1) then calls ed_gstage:(2)
